<title>UK: Hyder to invest 5 mln stg in rail consortium.</title>
<headline>Hyder to invest 5 mln stg in rail consortium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Multi-utility Hyder Plc said it would invest five million stg in City Greenwich Lewisham Rail Link Plc, the consortium that won the concession to build an extension to London's Docklands Light Railway (DLR).</p>
<p>A total 12.5 million stg will be invested by sponsors of the project company in which Hyder has a 40 percent stake.</p>
<p>The extension will link Lewisham and Greenwich, both south of the Thames, to the Isle of Dogs on the other side.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
